<%#
  Dismiss ✕ for a flash toast.

  Mandatory for the error variant, which no longer auto-dismisses — a persistent
  toast with no visible way to close it would be worse than the timer bug it
  replaces. The whole toast was already click-to-dismiss (flash_controller binds a
  click listener on its element), but with no affordance to reveal that; this is
  the missing affordance, not new behaviour.

  Rendered on the notice variant too so the two toasts don't diverge visually in
  the same slot — harmless there, since the click already dismissed them.

  Reuses the app's existing ✕: fa-xmark + aria-label, same as the card modal's
  close button (cards/show.html.erb) and the shortcuts overlay's. No Esc binding —
  Esc already has three claimants (modal, help overlay, filter popover) and a
  fourth risks that chain.

  `currentColor` inheritance means one partial works on both the crimson error and
  the pale success background without hardcoding either.
%>
<button type="button"
        class="shrink-0 -my-2 -mr-3 h-11 w-11 flex items-center justify-center rounded opacity-70 hover:opacity-100 bg-transparent border-0 cursor-pointer text-current focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-current focus-visible:ring-offset-1"
        aria-label="Dismiss">
  <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</button>
